{title: My Soul Sings (FJ_101_en)}
{song_number: 101}
{language: en}
{tempo: 85}
{artist: Samuel Harfst und Tobias Hundt}
{comment: English working translation of the German text; not an authorized original lyric or verified singable adaptation.}

{comment: Verse 1}
[Em]In the darkest of nights, [Bm]light began to shine.
[Am]You spoke a word, [Bm]and the darkness withdrew.
[Em]The water of life, [Bm]the source of the seas,
[Am]you made the heavens [Bm]and fashioned the mountains. [Em][D/F#]

{comment: Verse 2}
[Em]On the first day [Bm]your wind began to blow,
[Am]clothing all things in color [Bm]like a child with a brush.
[Em]A loving king [Bm]watched over the earth.
[Am]All creation [Bm]gave you the honor. [Em][D/F#]

{comment: Chorus}
[G]My soul is singing, oh, [Bm7]my soul is singing, [C]
[Dsus4]as long as I have breath. [G]Stars are shining bright for
[Bm7]you; the sea reflects their [C]light.
Oh, [Dsus4]my soul sings. [G]

{comment: Bridge}
[G]Holy, [Am7]holy, [C]holy are [G]you.
[G]How could I [Am7]be silent [C]when all things [G]cry?
[G]Holy, [Am7]holy, [C]holy are [G]you.
[G]How could I [Am7]be silent [C]when all things [G]cry?
